<h2 id=3D"1">betacalendars 1.0.0 =E2=80=94 deterministic date and calendar =
utilities</h2>
<div class=3D"outline-text-2" id=3D"text-1">
<p>
Archive: <a href=3D"https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/ann-betacalendars-1-0-0-det=
erministic-date-and-calendar-utilities/18593/1">https://discuss.ocaml.org/t=
/ann-betacalendars-1-0-0-deterministic-date-and-calendar-utilities/18593/1<=
/a>
</p>
</div>
<div id=3D"outline-container-orgb884c1b" class=3D"outline-3">
<h3 id=3D"orgb884c1b">Beta Calendars announced</h3>
<div class=3D"outline-text-3" id=3D"text-orgb884c1b">
<p>
I=E2=80=99m happy to announce the first stable release of <b>betacalendars<=
/b>, an OCaml library for timezone-independent civil-date arithmetic and de=
terministic calendar generation.
</p>

<p>
The library provides Gregorian date operations, configurable month and year=
 grids, bounded recurrence rules, and date-range and calendar-boundary util=
ities. It is designed for predictable date-only work without relying on loc=
al time zones.
</p>

<p>
Install it with opam:
</p>

<pre class=3D"example" id=3D"orgaa01652">
opam update
opam install betacalendars
</pre>

<ul class=3D"org-ul">
<li>Source: <a href=3D"https://github.com/mateopedersen/betacalendars-ocaml=
">https://github.com/mateopedersen/betacalendars-ocaml</a></li>
<li>Release: <a href=3D"https://github.com/mateopedersen/betacalendars-ocam=
l/releases/tag/v1.0.0">https://github.com/mateopedersen/betacalendars-ocaml=
/releases/tag/v1.0.0</a></li>
<li>API docs: <a href=3D"https://mateopedersen.github.io/betacalendars-ocam=
l/">https://mateopedersen.github.io/betacalendars-ocaml/</a></li>
<li>opam package metadata: <a href=3D"https://github.com/ocaml/opam-reposit=
ory/blob/master/packages/betacalendars/betacalendars.1.0.0/opam">https://gi=
thub.com/ocaml/opam-repository/blob/master/packages/betacalendars/betacalen=
dars.1.0.0/opam</a></li>
</ul>

<p>
The package has been tested with OCaml 4.14 and 5.5, including its test sui=
te and generated documentation. Feedback and questions are welcome.
</p>
</div>
