<h2 id=3D"2">Sedlex 3.8.1</h2>
<div class=3D"outline-text-2" id=3D"text-2">
<p>
Archive: <a href=3D"https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/ann-sedlex-3-8-1/18595/1">h=
ttps://discuss.ocaml.org/t/ann-sedlex-3-8-1/18595/1</a>
</p>
</div>
<div id=3D"outline-container-org7b37b56" class=3D"outline-3">
<h3 id=3D"org7b37b56">Hhugo announced</h3>
<div class=3D"outline-text-3" id=3D"text-org7b37b56">
<p>
Sedlex 3.8.1 is out! =F0=9F=8E=89
</p>

<p>
Sedlex is a unicode-friendly lexer generator for OCaml originally written by
Alain Frisch at LexiFi and now maintained under the
<a href=3D"https://github.com/ocaml-community">ocaml-community</a> umbrella.
</p>

<p>
The headline feature is <b>named capture groups</b>. Sub-patterns can be bo=
und
with OCaml's <code>as</code> syntax and read back in the action:
</p>

<div class=3D"org-src-container">
<pre class=3D"src src-ocaml"><code><span style=3D"color: #006f00; font-weig=
ht: bold;">match</span><span style=3D"color: #a7601f;">%sedlex</span> buf <=
span style=3D"color: #006f00; font-weight: bold;">with</span>
| (<span style=3D"color: #242521;">Plus</span> (<span style=3D"color: #ca34=
00;">'0'</span>..<span style=3D"color: #ca3400;">'9'</span>) <span style=3D=
"color: #006f00; font-weight: bold;">as</span> num), <span style=3D"color: =
#ca3400;">'.'</span>, (<span style=3D"color: #242521;">Plus</span> (<span s=
tyle=3D"color: #ca3400;">'0'</span>..<span style=3D"color: #ca3400;">'9'</s=
pan>) <span style=3D"color: #006f00; font-weight: bold;">as</span> frac) -&=
gt;
    <span style=3D"color: #242521; font-weight: bold;">let</span> <span sty=
le=3D"color: #007a9f;">n</span> =3D <span style=3D"color: #557400; font-wei=
ght: bold;">Sedlexing.Utf8.</span>of_submatch num <span style=3D"color: #24=
2521; font-weight: bold;">in</span>
    <span style=3D"color: #242521; font-weight: bold;">let</span> <span sty=
le=3D"color: #007a9f;">f</span> =3D <span style=3D"color: #557400; font-wei=
ght: bold;">Sedlexing.Utf8.</span>of_submatch frac <span style=3D"color: #2=
42521; font-weight: bold;">in</span>
    <span style=3D"color: #557400; font-weight: bold;">Printf.</span>printf=
 <span style=3D"color: #ca3400;">"integer=3D%s fractional=3D%s\n"</span> n f
| _ -&gt; ()
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>
Captures are implemented with a tagged DFA, so the generated lexer remains a
single pass with no backtracking, and lexers that don't use <code>as</code>=
 generate the
same code as before. Sub-matches are leftmost-greedy within the longest mat=
ch.
<code>as</code> is not allowed under <code>Star</code>, <code>Plus</code>, =
<code>Opt</code>, <code>Rep</code>, <code>Compl</code>, <code>Sub</code> or
<code>Intersect</code>.
</p>

<p>
This release also brings, among other things:
</p>

<ul class=3D"org-ul">
<li>Unicode 18.0.0</li>
<li>Faster <code>lexeme</code>, <code>sub_lexeme</code> and <code>of_submat=
ch</code> for Latin1, UTF-8 and UTF-16</li>
</ul>

<p>
