<div id=3D"outline-container-4" class=3D"outline-2">
<h2 id=3D"4">shakuhachi v0.4.0</h2>
<div class=3D"outline-text-2" id=3D"text-4">
<p>
Archive: <a href=3D"https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/ann-shakuhachi-v0-4-0/18599=
/1">https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/ann-shakuhachi-v0-4-0/18599/1</a>
</p>
</div>
<div id=3D"outline-container-org7c13fc7" class=3D"outline-3">
<h3 id=3D"org7c13fc7">EruEri announced</h3>
<div class=3D"outline-text-3" id=3D"text-org7c13fc7">
<p>
Dear all,
</p>

<p>
I=E2=80=99m happy to announce the release of shakuhachi v0.4.0.
</p>

<p>
Shakuhachi is still a music collection manager.
</p>

<p>
This release implements the 2 mains missing bits:
</p>
<ul class=3D"org-ul">
<li><p>
Query float/date property from the command line=20=20
</p>
<pre class=3D"example" id=3D"org12b8523">
# example:  List all musics of *Googgosh* played within the last 24 hour
$ skhc list %played_at:1dago..now %artist:Googoosh
# Or with the S-expression syntax
$ skhc list -Q "(and %played_at:1dago..now %artist:Googoosh)"
</pre></li>
<li><p>
Complex stats are finally computed when querying an artist
</p>
<pre class=3D"example" id=3D"orga75d903">
# example: List all artists having at least two albums
$ skhc list -Iartist %album_count:2..
</pre></li>
</ul>

<p>
This release also supports more&hellip; a sensible tagging/writing properti=
es.
</p>
<ul class=3D"org-ul">
<li>When adding a music the property <i>ALBUMARTISTS</i> (resp. <i>ARTISTS<=
/i>) will be looked first and fallback to <i>*ALBUMARTIST</i> (resp. <i>*AR=
TIST</i>).</li>
<li>When tagging, two new options <i>-j</i> and <i>-J</i> which set a joinp=
hrase between the name of  artists and artists of albums</li>
</ul>
<pre class=3D"example" id=3D"org61c55fd">
$ skhc tag -a "Sona Jobarteh" -j '&amp;' -a "Youssou N'Dour" Kambengwo.flac
# Will set ARTIST as a single value and ARTISTS as value containing two val=
ues
# ARTIST =3D Sona Jobarteh &amp; Youssou N'Dour
# ARTISTS =3D Sona Jobarteh | Youssou N'Dour
</pre>

<p>
<a href=3D"https://codeberg.org/EruEri/shakuhachi">https://codeberg.org/Eru=
Eri/shakuhachi</a>
</p>

<p>
Thanks you for your time
Sincerely yours.
</p>
</div>
